From de0ce7e8b2ef8a64ddf9a1c517d910a72dc4e469 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 13:29:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 23/54] kaiair: LDP deadline abandonment - stale retxs
 cancelled, slots go to new data (T-LDP.2 increments 1+2)

- base_harq_process gains kaiair_slot_first_tx (packet age reference; slot_tx moves per retx).
- ldp_deadline_slots(cfg, slots_per_ms) converts the LDP deadline to the cell numerology.
- Both intra-slice retx loops abandon (cancel_retxs) any pending retx whose packet age
  exceeds the deadline, per LDP-TR Definition 1 (post-deadline packets are dropped).
- HW-verified on the bench (KAIAIR_PKTR_DEADLINE_MS=10): abandonments fire at age 30
  slots >= 20-slot deadline with the link healthy. Bench truth: first UL retx opportunity
  on the P5 TDD config is ~15 ms after first tx, so ldp retx_interval_ms should be set
  ~15 (env KAIAIR_PKTR_RETX_MS) for an honest N(D) budget.
- 8/8 LDP unit tests pass.
